WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.769
House Republicans are at

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.471
what is supposed to be a policy retreat

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.405
right now in Florida.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.707
But yet again, under a Trump cloud,

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.309
the event was meant to deliver

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:09.776
focus

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.244
on delivering on their policy promises.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:11.945
Now, though,

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.780
more and more Republicans at that meeting

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.248
responding to the former president's

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.182
claims that he believes

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.951
he's about to be indicted this morning.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:18.585
Jim Jordan,

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.319
who is the chairman

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.253
of the Judiciary Committee,

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.955
going on conservative TV

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:22.522
to say he's

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.456
asking the Manhattan

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.424
district attorney

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.392
to testify

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.594
behind closed doors to his committee,

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.129
that after Kevin McCarthy, the House

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:29.896
speaker, vowed

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:32.032
Republicans would go on offense

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:32.766
for Trump.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:33.666
Our great reporters

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.501
are back to the table.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.636
And so let's listen to Jim Jordan again.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:37.470
Donald Trump

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.572
says he expects to be indicted

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.041
and arrested this week.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.342
We don't know if that's going to happen.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:42.842
We're waiting.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.443
But already

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.411
Jim Jordan says

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.012
to the Manhattan district attorney,

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:46.913
I want to talk to you

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.515
behind closed doors for an interview

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.618
President Trump announced

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:53.620
he was going to run for president again.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.121
And suddenly, here they go.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.256
Now they're coming after him

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:58.425
for some alleged bookkeeping error.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.126
You've got to be kidding me.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.995
So we want to know

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.096
what kind of federal involvement

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.298
may have may have taken place.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.933
It's the last part.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.334
Jordan's a master at this.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.903
What is is a New York

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.938
Manhattan local prosecutor?

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.473
We want to know

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.241
what kind of federal involvement

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.242
may have taken place.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.010
Is there any evidence

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.111
of federal involvement here?

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.512
Well, that was my initial question

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.480
when I saw the letter,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.848
because obviously Congress

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.650
generally has jurisdiction

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.351
over federal issues, federal matters.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.686
But this Manhattan D.A.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.954
is a state official

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.456
at the local official.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.291
So, you know, Jordan's

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.892
kind of putting out this wink, wink,

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.028
nudge nudge thing out in the ether.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:35.695
But broadly

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.529
speaking, it's

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.665
just it's really remarkable

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.333
how House Republicans

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.302
are really using the levers of government

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:45.338
that they have to defend Trump as as

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.340
as the president may or may not face

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.508
this indictment this week.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.409
And I think that

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.245
perhaps Speaker McCarthy feels

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.346
he has no other choice.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.048
We saw how reliant he is

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.316
on that Trump flank

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.550
to keep his speakership.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.319
But it really is a new level

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.053
what is going on here.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.521
And that's what makes it so interesting.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:01.921
If you're Jim

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.288
Jordan, you've

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.257
got a very reliably Republican district.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.959
So this is safe for you, right?

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.826
Standing up for Donald

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.261
Trump is actually good for you.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.295
Back home.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.430
Kevin McCarthy, as you know

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.197
it, is dependent on that

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:11.731
right flank

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.966
that made him speaker, including

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:13.867
Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.101
We'll get to her in a minute.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.069
But interestingly,

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:16.736
Kevin McCarthy

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.904
says we want to investigate

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:18.571
the investigator.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.973
We will use our power to look into

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.540
what's happening here.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.842
But he didn't make one distinction

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:23.343
from Trump.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.210
Trump, in one of his posts

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:24.744
over the weekend

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.546
said he wanted his supporters to protest.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.181
Kevin McCarthy says, please don't.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:30.250
I don't think

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.051
people should protest this now.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.020
And I think President Trump,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.654
if you talk to him,

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:35.989
he doesn't believe that either.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.390
We want calmness out there.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.658
Nobody

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:39.993
nobody

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.395
for violence or harm to anything else.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.533
And that is a key distinction borne of

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.434
memories of January 6th

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.736
Not no matter how much House Republicans

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.137
want to whitewash it.

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.806
And the idea that if it gets violent

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.509
or protests, that might hurt the party.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:56.809
Yes.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:57.510
I mean, that

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.678
that exactly is borne

00:02:58.678 --> 00:02:59.779
out of the memory of January six.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.648
We saw what happened there as Trump

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.282
fanned the flames

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.216
and many of his allies said,

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.318
and here we have Republicans saying

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.486
pump the brakes a little bit.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:09.589
We have eight, 18 or so House Republicans

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.624
who are in districts won by Biden.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:12.158
Right.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.194
Where that kind of rhetoric, that kind of

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.563
fire fiery rhetoric doesn't

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.031
necessarily play as well as voters there.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:18.798
And so, you know,

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:19.832
this is the kind of tricky line

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.767
Republicans are going to have

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:21.901
to walk on this.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.703
And Marjorie Taylor Greene, again, key

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.471
to Kevin McCarthy speakership.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.940
She was asked over the weekend

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:27.507
People were saying,

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:27.874
you know, Trump

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:28.841
didn't say peaceful protest.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:29.475
He said protests.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.276
And she said, of course,

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.177
he meant that Americans

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.045
have the right to assemble

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:32.912
and the right to protest.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.380
Trump doesn't have to say peaceful

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.448
for him to mean peaceful.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.849
Of course he means peaceful

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.752
She's not opposed to protests.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:40.620
No, she's not.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.521
And I mean,

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.022
for Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.691
she's one of the staunchest Trump

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.726
Trump allies in the House

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:47.994
and she's going to

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:48.962
she's defending him

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.463
and defending the right to protest

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.532
and defending his calls to protest.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:53.132
I just find it

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.268
so interesting that House members,

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:55.868
that wink

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.469
sung members

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:57.036
talking about it

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.504
because it's that wink of,

00:03:58.504 --> 00:03:59.172
you know,

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.907
looking into the weaponization

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.342
of the federal government,

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.409
but in the process

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.311
weaponizing the federal government

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.313
to defend former President Trump,

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.047
people like Marjorie

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:08.648
Taylor Greene

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:09.949
are all for that,

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.418
but also all for Trump's calls

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.254
for whatever happens in the streets,

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:14.721
of course,

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:15.455
but given themselves

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:17.123
plausible deniability

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.392
should anything become violent.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.060
If the House Republicans

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.061
proceed with this,

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.696
they sent the letters to Alvin Bragg.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:24.931
We'll see how the case plays out.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.532
We'll see how the Congress plays out.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.300
Hakeem Jeffries,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.167
the Democratic leader, says

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.102
Democrats will participate

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:29.636
and push back

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:30.603
as aggressively as possible.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.037
But listen here.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.038
This is Mark Kelly,

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.539
Democratic senator from Arizona,

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.374
just reelected.

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.042
So he's got a six year term

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:36.876
not a lot to worry about

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:37.677
in the short term.

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.312
He says this is dangerous for the

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.179
Manhattan prosecutor.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:42.682
I would hope that if

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:43.549
they brought charges

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.585
that they have a strong case

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.954
because this is, as you said,

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.222
it's unprecedented.

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:49.922
And, you know,

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.158
there are certainly risks involved here.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.162
But again, nobody in our nation is

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.231
or should be above the law.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.232
Very careful there.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.400
Nobody is above the law.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.567
Very clear about that.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.502
But a guy, a Democrat

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.636
from a purple state, again,

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.771
even though he's got six years for.

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.205
Yes, go back for the voters,

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:06.973
essentially saying,

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.474
please be careful here. Right.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.509
And it'd be interesting

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.444
for him to elaborate on what risks mean.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.045
Like there

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:13.780
certainly could be a political risk

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.181
for Democrats here.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.416
Perhaps not, because, again,

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:17.550
this is unprecedented.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.052
It is an indictment

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.787
of a former president.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:22.588
It comes at a time when Republicans

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.390
were already turning from the party.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.658
But obviously you know,

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.126
just physical risk as well.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:27.994
And hopefully,

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.529
you know, things remain calm.

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.664
And that remains the case.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.032
And the key to that is we wait.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:33.566
We wait that

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:34.767
it is, again, Donald Trump saying

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:35.802
he expects to be indicted

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:36.669
and arrested tomorrow.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.004
We do not know that we will watch

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:39.072
the investigation play out.

